---
title: useCopyToClipboard
description: Copy text with the Clipboard API and keep temporary feedback in local Svelte state.
---

<p class="eyebrow">Svelte pattern</p>

# useCopyToClipboard

<CopyMarkdownButton url="/docs/hooks/use-copy-to-clipboard.md" />

The upstream React page provides a hook with copied state and a reset timeout. COSS for Svelte does
not export a `useCopyToClipboard` hook. Clipboard state belongs to the component that presents the
feedback, and Svelte's local state is enough for that job.

## Basic

```svelte
<button type="button" onclick={() => void navigator.clipboard.writeText("https://coss.com")}>
  Copy
</button>
```

## Temporary feedback

Invalidate an earlier copy before starting the next one. The generation and abort signal prevent an
old clipboard request from updating state after a later click or after the component unmounts.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { onDestroy } from "svelte";

  const timeout = 2000;
  let copied = $state(false);
  let timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;
  let controller: AbortController | undefined;
  let destroyed = false;
  let generation = 0;

  function isCurrent(operation: number, signal: AbortSignal): boolean {
    return !destroyed && operation === generation && !signal.aborted;
  }

  function destroy(): void {
    destroyed = true;
    generation += 1;
    controller?.abort();
    controller = undefined;
    clearTimeout(timer);
  }

  async function copy(value: string): Promise<void> {
    if (destroyed || !value || !navigator.clipboard?.writeText) return;

    const operation = ++generation;
    controller?.abort();
    const requestController = new AbortController();
    controller = requestController;

    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(value);
    if (!isCurrent(operation, requestController.signal)) return;

    clearTimeout(timer);
    copied = true;
    timer = setTimeout(() => {
      if (!isCurrent(operation, requestController.signal)) return;
      copied = false;
      timer = undefined;
    }, timeout);
  }

  onDestroy(destroy);
</script>
```

Set no timer when the copied state should remain true until the component unmounts.

## Callback after a successful copy

Run a callback only after `writeText` resolves and the operation is still current. A rejected or
invalidated clipboard request must not report a successful copy.

```ts
await navigator.clipboard.writeText(value);
if (!isCurrent(operation, requestController.signal)) return;
copied = true;
onCopy?.();
```

## With an icon swap

Use the shared SSR-safe renderer with Hugeicons data.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { Copy01Icon, Tick01Icon } from "@hugeicons/core-free-icons";
  import { Button, HugeiconsIcon } from "@coss-sv/ui";
  import { onDestroy } from "svelte";

  let copied = $state(false);
  let timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;
  let controller: AbortController | undefined;
  let destroyed = false;
  let generation = 0;

  function isCurrent(operation: number, signal: AbortSignal): boolean {
    return !destroyed && operation === generation && !signal.aborted;
  }

  function destroy(): void {
    destroyed = true;
    generation += 1;
    controller?.abort();
    controller = undefined;
    clearTimeout(timer);
  }

  async function copy(value: string): Promise<void> {
    if (destroyed || !value || !navigator.clipboard?.writeText) return;

    const operation = ++generation;
    controller?.abort();
    const requestController = new AbortController();
    controller = requestController;

    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(value);
    if (!isCurrent(operation, requestController.signal)) return;

    clearTimeout(timer);
    copied = true;
    timer = setTimeout(() => {
      if (!isCurrent(operation, requestController.signal)) return;
      copied = false;
      timer = undefined;
    }, 2_000);
  }

  onDestroy(destroy);
</script>

<Button
  aria-label="Copy to clipboard"
  onclick={() => copy("https://coss.com")}
  size="icon"
  variant="outline"
>
  <HugeiconsIcon aria-hidden="true" icon={copied ? Tick01Icon : Copy01Icon} strokeWidth={2} />
</Button>
```

## Error handling

Clipboard access can fail when the page is not served from a secure context or the browser denies
permission. Catch the error when the interface needs to report that failure. Do not flip the copied
state until `writeText` resolves.
